A||||5||cscougar||CD & Subwoofer Question
Z||000000||cscougar||08-12-99||04:32 PM||||I have a Pioneer Supertuner Radio/CD that I am going to put in my 85 SE.  It has a factory pushbutton Radio/Cassette with the factory subwoofer right now.  Is there a trick to hooking up this pioneer radio to the subwoofer to make things work...or do I just plug things in with an adapter?<p>Thanks,<p>Ted
Z||000001||DJRice||08-13-99||07:04 AM||||The best way is just to get one of those quick install wiring harness that will plug into the factory wiring. As I recall, but it has been a long time since I have been under my dash, the Subwoofer wiring plugged into  the car wiring which plugged into the radio.  Those quick install harnesses are usually less than $10us and allow you to do the wiring and crimping or soldering at a table or bench instead of hunched over in the car.  You almost can go wrong that way if you follow the instructions.
Z||000002||batboy||08-13-99||01:23 PM||||Cougar, are you planning on using a  different aftermarket amp or trying to hook into the factory amp? I believe the factory subwoofer amp was mounted under the console. You are going to have to connect the RCA outlets in the back of the CD player to the sub amp (factory or aftermarket) by either swapping in the right wiring adaptors or splicing the correct terminals onto the wires. There is a short article about installing stereos in the brand new FOCOA magazine where they mention wiring in the subwoofer.
Z||000003||cscougar||08-13-99||02:31 PM||||Batboy,<p>Is there anyway you can scan in the instructions or repeat them someway so I will understand how to hook up the subwoofer without blowing the factory amp?<p>Thanks,<p>Ted
Z||000004||batboy||08-14-99||09:24 AM||||Cougar, I sent you an email with two attachments containing that two page stereo article. The files were bigger than I expected, so I hope you will get them ok. Let me know if I should split the two files up and resend it as two separate emails or send it by snail mail. Good luck.
Z||000005||Orlando||08-19-99||07:17 PM||||If you're going to install the pioneer head unit, and keep the factory sub/amp, all you need to do is to call Crutchfield for one of thier adapter kits. Tell them you have the factory sub/amp setup and you want to use it with your new radio. The sell a complete kit with a wiring harness and a relay so you can use the factory sub for under $20. It also comes with tons of diagrams and instructions. Real easy to install.
